# The routing-generation entry is kept in memory only. A WAL shard restart
# loses the fence a close raised, so a write admitted before the close is
# allocated above the recorded head, and the owner passes it.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestGenerationNotDurable
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a WAL shard restart loses the routing-generation entry
PERTURBS: Restart
BOUNDS: WithRestart = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ UNCHANGED fFence
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the generation entry is not durable.
    /\ fFence' = 1
--- END
